title: Diagnosing a slow operation
tags: [[Slow log]]
kind: guide
summary: Read the slow log with mf slow, find where the time went, and replay a query to see whether it still goes there.

!! Read the log

```
mf slow                    # the newest entries, both processes merged
mf slow list --since 2h    # only the last two hours (-d; 30m, 7d…)
mf slow list --op query    # only operations whose name contains "query"
```

Each entry is a header line — when it started, how long it took, which process
timed it (`daemon` or `gui`), the operation — then its context and its phases,
indented by nesting:

```
2026-09-09 14:03:22  4.82s  daemon  POST /repos/:repo/query
    client    mfr_path ->* "/2024" and rating > 3
    results   1240
    keys      210 314
    wait:conn         3.10s
    prepare           1.65s       210 008 keys
    index.evaluate      40ms           306 keys
```

`--json` prints the raw entries, one per line, for a script
([[What the slow log records]]).

!! Where the time went

* ''Read the phases, not the total.'' The total says it was slow, which you knew.
* A `wait:conn` phase is time spent waiting for the repository, which something else was holding — a reconcile, a watcher flush. The operation itself was fine.
* A phase that took long and read few keys ''waited'' — for a lock, a cold disk cache, a loaded machine. One that read many keys did the work.
* Time not covered by any phase is code that is not instrumented: that is where to look.
* A GUI entry and a daemon entry with the same id are one request seen from both sides: 4.9 s in the GUI against 0.2 s in the daemon means the time went to the client ([[Correlating the GUI and the daemon]]).

!! Replay a query

```
mf slow replay                  # the newest logged query, run again now
mf slow replay --at <at_ms>     # the one logged at that time
mf slow replay -q '<query>'     # any query (-s for simplified text)
```

prints the same breakdown for the query run ''now''
([[POST /repos/:repo/query/profile]]). A `wait:conn` that dominated the entry and
is gone from the replay was the diagnosis: something else held the repository.
A phase whose reads stayed the same while its time did not waited on the disk
or the machine, not on the query.

To reproduce a slowdown on purpose, start from an empty log: `mf slow clear`.
